Disable Certificate Validation in IntelliJ
Go to Run/Debug Configurations:

In IntelliJ, click on Run > Edit Configurations.
Add JVM Options:

In the VM Options field, add:
text
Copy code
-Dcom.sun.net.ssl.checkRevocation=false -Djavax.net.ssl.trustStoreType=Dummy
Save and Run:

Save the configuration and run your application.
----------------------
Disable Certificate Validation via Command Line
Add the following JVM option when running your application:

bash
Copy code
-Dcom.sun.net.ssl.checkRevocation=false -Djavax.net.ssl.trustStoreType=Dummy
This disables SSL certificate validation for the Java process.
